    "According to you, how can LLMs be used to innovate math learning in schools and universities?": "LLMs can offer personalized tutoring, explain concepts in simple language, and adapt to a student’s pace. They can provide instant feedback, make abstract ideas more relatable, and reduce anxiety. In universities, they could assist with problem-solving practice. For older learners like me, they offer a gentle, non-judgmental way to revisit math with confidence."
